# Sales

The Sales section provides an overview of your product sales and marketplace performance.

It helps you monitor revenue, identify trends, and better understand customer activity.

---

# Overview

Your sales dashboard provides information about:

- Total Sales
- Total Revenue
- Recent Orders
- Product Performance
- Customer Activity
- Sales History

Statistics may be updated periodically.

---

# Sales History

Your sales history includes records of completed purchases.

Typical information includes:

- Order ID
- Product Name
- Purchase Date
- License Type
- Sale Amount
- Order Status

Sales records should be retained for your reference.

---

# Revenue

Revenue represents the income generated from successful product sales.

Revenue information may include:

- Gross Revenue
- Marketplace Fees
- Net Earnings
- Pending Balance
- Paid Balance

The available information may change as new reporting features are introduced.

---

# Product Performance

You can use sales data to evaluate product performance.

Useful metrics include:

- Number of Sales
- Product Views
- Conversion Rate
- Customer Ratings
- Customer Reviews

Monitoring these metrics can help improve your products over time.

---

# Refunds

Approved refunds may affect your sales statistics and earnings.

Refund information will be recorded in your sales history where applicable.

---

# Reports

Sales reports may include:

- Daily Sales
- Weekly Sales
- Monthly Sales
- Yearly Sales

Additional reporting tools may become available in future releases.

---

# Best Practices

Successful sellers typically:

- Monitor sales regularly.
- Keep products updated.
- Respond to customer questions promptly.
- Improve products based on customer feedback.
- Maintain accurate product information.

